18386129167305698,"_gp_margin_vs_hist":true,"_score_margin_vs_hist":77.0,"_gate_piotroski":4,"_gp_piotroski":false,"_score_piotroski":44.4,"_gate_spread":0.005453141598959807,"_gp_spread":false,"_score_spread":2.7,"_gate_roic_consistency":0.14228190866263696,"_gp_roic_consistency":true,"_score_roic_consistency":76.3,"_gate_incr_roic":0.06548599515692627,"_gp_incr_roic":false,"_score_incr_roic":38.5,"_gate_margin_advantage":0.017921932900681226,"_gp_margin_advantage":false,"_score_margin_advantage":39.3,"_gate_pool_share":-0.014712487013554987,"_gp_pool_share":false,"_score_pool_share":34.1,"_gate_rev_durability":0.028032928078012276,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":39.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":0.0,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":0.0,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.021028649830194368,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":34.5,"_gate_share_shrink":0.009001420140977379,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":38.7,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.00443754756916523,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":92.6,"_gate_insider_own":0.00329,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":2.2,"_gate_insider_buying":1.0,"_gp_insider_buying":true,"_score_insider_buying":100.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"MGE Energy, Inc., through its subsidiaries, operates as a public utility holding company in the United States. It operates through Regulated Electric Utility Operations; Regulated Gas Utility Operations; Nonregulated Energy Operations; Transmission Investments; and All Other segments. The company generates, purchases, and distributes electricity; purchases and distributes natural gas; owns and leases electric generating capacity; and plans, constructs, operates, maintains, and expands transmission facilities to provide transmission power services. It also generates electricity from coal-fired, gas-fired, and renewable energy sources and provides solar and wind generation, and battery storage services. As of December 31, 2025, the company owned and operated 811 miles of overhead electric distribution lines; 1,386 miles of underground electric distribution cables; 47 substations with an installed capacity of 1.2 million kVA; and gas facilities, including 3,117 miles of distribution mains, as well as supplied electric service to approximately 170,000 customers. MGE Energy, Inc. has a strategic partnership with Realta Fusion Inc. and Madison Gas and Electric Company. MGE Energy, Inc. was incorporated in 2001 and is headquartered in Madison, Wisconsin.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Jeffrey M. Keebler | President, CEO & Chairman of the Board | Age 53 | Compensation: $1.7M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 726 people. Revenue per employee of $1.0M ranks in the above the sector median among Utilities peers. Stock-based compensation of $5K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 2\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (1/10).","financial_summary":["MGE Energy Inc. is a mid-cap utilities business with a $3.0B market cap on $744M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +1% over the past three years and +3% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 7% against a 6% cost of capital, which means the business barely earns its keep economically.","The company is burning through $80M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 5.3\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and interest coverage runs at 4.8\u00d7.","Shareholder yield of 2.1% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 62% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.6223141490407997},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.7) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 5.8% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Regulatory rate-case risk and rising cost of capital \u2014 the allowed return is set by commissions, and the business lives or dies by that negotiation.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Grid modernisation capex burden \u2014 aging infrastructure requires massive reinvestment that regulators may not fully allow into rate base, compressing earned returns.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Wildfire and climate liability \u2014 extreme weather events create catastrophic, uninsurable losses that can push even investment-grade utilities toward restructuring.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Returns on capital have been remarkably steady for 5 years \u2014 durability is the real test of a moat","Insiders are net buyers (100% buy ratio) \u2014 insiders sell for many reasons but buy for only one","39 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Utilities sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter","Utilities tends to hold up well as investors rotate into defensive names"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Will Earnings Beat Change MGE Energy (MGEE) Narrative","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/utilities/nasdaq-mgee/mge-energy/news/will-earnings-beat-change-mge-energy-mgee-narrative","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793875099.985,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.818,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Why MGE (MGEE) is a Great Dividend Stock Right Now","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3023231/why-mge-mgee-is-a-great-dividend-stock-right-now?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7Cyseop_template_5-3023231","date":"2026-11-04","timestamp":1793807101.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.625,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["dividend"]},{"title":"MGE (MGEE) Q3 Earnings and Revenues Top Estimates","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3023098/mge-mgee-q3-earnings-and-revenues-top-estimates?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7Cyseop_template_4-3023098","date":"2026-11-04","timestamp":1793801102.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.202,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"MGE Energy (MGEE) Rebounds In The Short Term, Does It Look Fairly Valued?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/utilities/nasdaq-mgee/mge-energy/news/mge-energy-mgee-rebounds-in-the-short-term-does-it-look-fair","date":"2026-11-04","timestamp":1793784450.031,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.827,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Trading Systems Reacting to (MGEE) Volatility","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/11/Trading_Systems_Reacting_to_MGEE_Volatility_110226121804_1793639884.html","date":"2026-11-02","timestamp":1793639884.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.273,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"MGE Energy Releases Investor Presentation Ahead of 2026 EEI Financial Conference","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/news/ann